---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice | EL-Desk"
  description="Data handling, retention, and transport security details for the private EL-Desk remote desktop deployment."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:px-8">
    <header class="border-b border-[var(--border)] pb-8">
      <div class="font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--accent-text)]">
        Privacy Notice
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,2.75rem)] font-bold leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.025em] text-[var(--text)]">
        EL-Desk <em class="font-serif font-normal italic text-[var(--accent-text)]">privacy notice</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        Scope: private EL-Desk remote desktop deployment (1 to 5 personal accounts).
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="divide-y divide-[var(--border)] text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text)]">
      <section class="py-7 space-y-2.5">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent-text)]">01 / ACCOUNT DATA</div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">
          Stored account and audit data
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
          The private EL-Desk API (routed via Cloudflare Worker and VPS Caddy to the Go API) stores
          login credentials (bcrypt password hashes), personal address books, device tags, and
          session audit timestamps inside the owner's NeonDB PostgreSQL instance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="py-7 space-y-2.5">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent-text)]">02 / PRESENCE</div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">
          Transient presence heartbeats
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
          Device heartbeat checks keep peer online status in Go process memory with a 45-second
          expiration window. Heartbeat payloads are never written to PostgreSQL. The{" "}
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--text)]">hbbs</span> rendezvous process maintains peer
          routing identifiers locally in SQLite on the VPS.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="py-7 space-y-2.5">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent-text)]">03 / TRANSPORT</div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">
          Encryption and third-party servers
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
          Client builds pin the private relay server and require public key verification (
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--text)]">-k _</span>) before establishing remote
          sessions. Builds do not transmit telemetry or update checks to public RustDesk
          infrastructure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="py-7 space-y-2.5">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent-text)]">04 / PORTAL</div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">
          Web portal requests
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
          This web portal sets no analytics trackers or advertising cookies. Local storage is used
          strictly to remember your chosen light or dark theme preference in the browser.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-7">
      <a
        href="/#downloads"
        class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-strong)] bg-[var(--surface)] px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text)] transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-[var(--surface-subtle)] no-underline"
      >
        <span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span>
        <span>Return to client downloads</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
